+# sibling CLAUDE.md symlink (the `pair` rule checks existence only; the
+# command checks link type and target) and run `scripts/check-no-python.sh`.
+# Alint runs command rules from the repository root and substitutes `{path}`
+# with the matched relative path, so the scanner runs once on its exact file.
 # Validate with the pinned alint binary: `alint validate-config`.
 # The 80-line function/method limit (§5, "using Clippy accounting") is NOT
 # expressed here — alint ships no function-level rule kind. It is enforced
@@ -62,6 +63,7 @@ rules:
